1. Her name is Elia Stellaria, and it literally means "L" due to her habit of taking "L's" in life. (Verbatim: "It literally means L. Yeah. It's just me taking L's and then being like, yeah, and yeah, yeah, mm-hmm.")
2. She has a long-distance relationship with her AirPods, which are currently in Los Angeles while she is in England. (Verbatim: "I'm in England, my AirPods are in LA.")
3. She once left her AirPods in Los Angeles during a trip to AX (Anime Expo). (Verbatim: "I went there for AX and I think I left it.")
4. She is known for buying multiple cat ears on Discord, which triggered automated security measures. (Verbatim: "Discord made me do a bunch of captures because apparently I bought too many cat ears on there.")
5. She humorously refers to herself as a robot due to her high number of capture attempts and frequent login issues. (Verbatim: "And it genuinely thought I was a robot.")
6. She has a strong aversion to being doxed and is cautious about revealing personal details publicly. (Verbatim: "Doxing is a serious issue. People be wild.")
7. She enjoys paninis and considers them a common item at coffee shops in England. (Verbatim: "Now you can get paninis from like every coffee shop in England, I would say.")
8. She has a habit of forgetting to eat, especially during intense work sessions, and trained herself to sleep instead. (Verbatim: "I remember thinking, 'Oh, what should I have for dinner?' 'Oh, nothing. I'll sleep.'")
9. She has a fondness for the word "L" and finds joy in her community chanting it. (Verbatim: "I love how chat just becomes L. Like you're all cheering for L.")
10. She learned the concept of "freedom" during a trip to America. (Verbatim: "This is what I learned from my time in America by the way if y'all were wondering like where I learned freedom from.") [end of text]



1. She wishes she had a house. (Verbatim: "I wish I had a house.")  
2. She enjoys singing, though she intentionally sings poorly during performances. (Verbatim: "Sorry, I'm singing terribly on purpose.")  
3. She has a fondness for performing song covers, specifically planning to do an English cover of "Any Time, Anywhere, the Free Run Ending." (Verbatim: "I'm gonna be doing a English cover of it.")  
4. She references her birthday in connection with a past event (Birthday Donathon), indicating she has a birthday celebration event. (Verbatim: "We picked what song cover we're going to do all the way from my Birthday Donathon.")  
5. She finds the concept of a "tavern" and roleplaying as a waitress entertaining and immersive. (Verbatim: "I'd be such a good waitress.")  
6. She is familiar with and references Twitch's color scheme, noting that game elements use the same colors. (Verbatim: "They pick the same colors as Twitch, that's so cool.")  
7. She mentions England as a place she’s familiar with, referencing local delivery services and measurement systems. (Verbatim: "In England, you can like order stuff on Amazon and it'll arrive the same day.")  
8. She uses centimeters as her preferred unit of measurement, though acknowledges others may use feet. (Verbatim: "I personally like to measure in centimeters, but I think most people in England use feet.")  
9. She describes her height as "normal tall-ish." (Verbatim: "I think I'm normal tall-ish.")  
10. She enjoys playing games that involve crafting, decorating, and managing a virtual tavern. (Verbatim: "Let's go. We cleaned up! A bit of the area!") [end of text]



1. She considers herself "normal tall-ish". (Verbatim: "I think I'm normal tall-ish.")
2. She has a close relationship with her 94-year-old grandmother who is tech-savvy and uses an iPad. (Verbatim: "she's, like, 94, she's very good with technology, she uses her iPad and everything")
3. Her grandmother is critical of Facebook, calling it full of fake news, conspiracies, and stupid people. (Verbatim: "she's, she, her rants about Facebook are wild. They're straight up like, people are so stupid, they're just absolutely stupid on there.")
4. She humorously imagines her grandmother thriving in future retirement homes equipped with full gaming setups. (Verbatim: "I think she would thrive and be like, you know, really heckin' good, she'd be like, the number first place at the LAN parties, for sure")
5. She jokes about wanting to be buried with her graphics card and refers to "yearning for the urn" and "craving the grave". (Verbatim: "I want to be buried with my graphics card, we yearn for the urn, yearn for the urn, yearn for the urn, crave the grave, crave the grave, yippee")
6. She identifies with the concept of the "seven deadly sins" and speculates that she might embody "wrath" or "pride" due to her potential for intense reactions when provoked. (Verbatim: "I think I'm wrath. Because, because, because I never rage. Which means, which means, oops. When I do rage, it'll be deadly sin level.")
7. She reflects on the idea that ambition and greed are closely tied for her, and she sometimes questions the line between the two. (Verbatim: "I don't know where the line is between ambitious and greedy. Yeah, I'm greedy.")
8. She has a self-deprecating sense of humor about her own personality, acknowledging she might be prideful and needing to "up my self-deprecation humor". (Verbatim: "Think I'm prideful. Think I'm proud. That sounds like we need to up my self-deprecation humor.")
9. She has a playful, recurring fantasy about VTubers being "old men" and imagines future retirement homes as high-tech gaming hubs. (Verbatim: "All VTubers are just old men. Yeah, can't confirm. All really, really, really, really old men.")
10. She expresses concern about her grandmother potentially being influenced by TikTok, fearing she might start speaking in "brain rot" or internet slang. (Verbatim: "what if next time, if I get her on TikTok, okay, and then the next time I see her, she only speaks in brain rot, and, and, and no one's gonna, like, understand") [end of text]



